 \\le Limit$. (Ignore if Limit=0).\\n   - Slack Bus: $\\theta_{ref} = 0$.\\n\\n5. Objective:\\n   - Minimize $\\sum Cost(P_g)$.\\n   - Note: Reserves usually have a cost too, but the problem description doesn't mention reserve costs, only \\\"economically efficient\\\". Usually this implies min Gen Cost. I'll assume Reserve Cost is 0 or negligible, but the constraint forces cheaper generation to back off if needed.\\n\\nImplementation details:\\n- Use `scipy.optimize.linprog` if costs are linear. If quadratic, `minimize` with SLSQP. `gencost` usually has 3 coefficients for quadratic. If $c_2=0$, it's linear.\\n- I'll check if costs are quadratic. If so, `minimize`. Note that `minimize` can be slow for 4000 vars. But `scipy`'s SLSQP is decent.\\n- Constructing sparse matrices for constraints is crucial for performance. `scipy.sparse` is available.\\n\\nLet's check the cost model first to decide between LP and QP.\",\n  \"plan\": \"1. Check the `gencost` coefficients to see if they are linear or quadratic.\\n2. Write the `solve_dcopf.py` script.\",\n  \"commands\": [\n    {\n      \"keystrokes\": \"source venv/bin/activate\\npython3 -c \\\"import json; d=json.load(open('network.json')); costs = d['gencost']; is_quadratic = any(c[3] == 3 for c in costs) if len(costs[0]) \u003e 3 else False; print('Is Quadratic:', is_quadratic); print('First cost:', costs[0])\\\"\\n\",\n      \"duration\": 1.0\n    }\n  ]\n}"
